<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="htmx-config" content='{"defaultTimeout":10000}'><title>Relay | Work moves better together</title><meta name="description" content="A complete HyperChi and Jet marketing example with server-rendered pricing."><link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/marketing.css"><script defer src="/static/js/htmx.min.js"></script><script defer src="/static/js/marketing.js"></script></head>
<body class="relay" id="top"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><div class="example-bar"><a href="/docs/integrations">← HyperChi examples</a><span>Jet + htmx</span><a href="/docs/jet">How this works ↗</a></div>
<header class="marketing-nav wrap"><a href="#top" class="wordmark">relay↗</a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="#workflow">Why Relay</a><a href="#pricing">Pricing</a><a href="#questions">Questions</a></nav></header>
<main id="main"><section class="relay-hero wrap"><div><p class="label">For teams who make things</p><h1>Less chasing.<br>More making.</h1><p>A shared place for the decisions, details, and next steps that keep good work moving.</p><a class="button" href="#workflow">Meet your new workflow ↗</a></div><img src="/static/img/examples/workspace.webp" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Sunlit meeting room with a long table and glass walls" fetchpriority="high"></section>
<section class="wrap relay-manifesto"><p>THE WORK IS NOT THE PROBLEM.</p><h2>It is everything<br>around the work.</h2><p class="large-copy">The brief in one tab. The feedback in another. The decision nobody can find. Relay puts the project back in one place.</p></section>
<section class="wrap" id="workflow"><h2>From first thought<br>to final handoff.</h2><div class="workflow-grid"><article><span class="step">01</span><h3>Set a direction</h3><p>Capture the brief, agree on the outcome, and give everyone a place to start.</p></article><article><span class="step">02</span><h3>Keep the context</h3><p>Put decisions beside the work. No digging through messages to understand what changed.</p></article><article><span class="step">03</span><h3>Move it forward</h3><p>Make the next step visible, assign an owner, and leave a useful handoff.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="wrap relay-features"><div><h2>A little structure.<br>A lot more space.</h2><p>Relay is a fictional product for teams who need a shared rhythm without turning every task into a process.</p></div><dl><div><dt>Project rooms</dt><dd>A permanent home for the brief, the files, and the decisions.</dd></div><div><dt>Considered updates</dt><dd>A digest that tells the story of what moved, what is next, and what needs attention.</dd></div><div><dt>Guest reviews</dt><dd>Bring a client into the conversation without bringing them into everything else.</dd></div><div><dt>Useful handoffs</dt><dd>Close a project with its context intact, ready for whoever picks it up next.</dd></div></dl></section>
<section class="wrap pricing-section" id="pricing"><p class="label">Room to start. Space to grow.</p><h2>A plan that fits<br>the way you work.</h2><p>Illustrative plans for this demo. No account, payment, or subscription is created.</p><form class="billing-form" method="get" action="/examples/jet#pricing" hx-get="/examples/jet/pricing" hx-target="#pricing-result" hx-indicator="#pricing-loading"><label for="billing">Billing period</label><select id="billing" name="billing"><option value="monthly" {{if .Billing == "monthly"}}selected{{end}}>Monthly</option><option value="annual" {{if .Billing == "annual"}}selected{{end}}>Annual · save two months</option></select><button class="button" type="submit">Update pricing</button><span class="htmx-indicator" id="pricing-loading" role="status">Updating…</span></form><p class="request-error" role="alert" hidden>Pricing could not be loaded. Please try again.</p><div id="pricing-result" aria-live="polite">{{include "pricing.jet"}}</div></section>
<section class="wrap relay-principles"><h2>Keep your focus.<br>Keep your context.</h2><p class="large-copy">A calmer working day starts when everyone knows where to look. Give your next project a shared home.</p><a class="text-link" href="#questions">Get to know Relay ↗</a></section>
<section class="wrap faq-section" id="questions"><h2>Before you move in.</h2><details open><summary>What is included in both plans?</summary><p>Both sample plans include project rooms, notes, files, and team digests. The studio plan adds guest review workflows.</p></details><details><summary>How does annual billing work?</summary><p>The annual option shows a monthly equivalent, with the full annual charge displayed beneath the plans. All prices are fictional.</p></details><details><summary>Can I actually sign up?</summary><p>Relay is a demonstration, so there is no signup or checkout. The pricing selector is a real request to a Go handler that renders a Jet fragment.</p></details></section></main>
<footer class="wrap marketing-footer"><a class="wordmark" href="#top">relay↗</a><p>Fictional product. Real server-rendered interaction.</p><a href="/docs/jet">Read the integration guide ↗</a></footer></body></html>
